# Capability terminology (ADR-0050 + ADR-0051)

**Capability** is the stable semantic noun. Bare **skill** is ambiguous — always qualify.

## One sentence

OASF skills **classify** capabilities; A2A AgentSkills **advertise** capabilities; Agent Skill packages **implement** procedural knowledge for capabilities.

## Layer map

| Layer | Term | Standards object |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Canonical | **CapabilityDefinition** | AP-owned semantic outcome |
| Classification | **OASF skill taxon** | OASF record taxonomy |
| Advertisement | **A2A AgentSkill** / **A2A advertised capability** | Agent Card `skills[]` |
| Playbook | **Agent Skill package** / **SKILL.md package** | Agent Skills standard |
| Operation | **MCP tool** | Typed executable invocation |
| Credential | **capability claim** / **SkillClaimCredential** | Private VC (spec 251) |

## Packages

| Package | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `@agenticprimitives/capability-claims` | Capability claim VCs + vocabulary types |
| `@agenticprimitives/agent-skills` | **Deprecated alias** — re-exports `capability-claims` |

`@agenticprimitives/capability-claims` is **not** Agent Skill packages (`SKILL.md`).

## Ontology

| Namespace | Canonical | Deprecated alias |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `aps:` | `CapabilityDefinition`, `CapabilityGrounding` | `AgentSkillDefinition`, `SkillGrounding` |
| `apguide:` | `AgentSkillPackage` | `AgentGuidanceSkill` |

## Style rule

Outside code implementing a particular standard's types, **skill must have a qualifier**.

| Avoid | Use |
| --- | --- |
| register the skill | register the **OASF skill taxon** / publish the **A2A AgentSkill** |
| load the skill | load the **Agent Skill package** |
| verify the skill | verify the **capability claim credential** |

## UI

Prefer **Capabilities** with sub-sections: advertised, classifications, runtime playbooks, operations, credentials.

**Source:** ADR-0051, vocabulary-map.md, spec 325 §2.2 (see agent-rules/README.md).

## The advertisement layer is CAPABILITY (ADR-0051, 2026-09-01)

Three names. One meaning each. They are not interchangeable and the collision between them is the whole
reason this rule exists.

| Name | What it is | Where the word `skills` is allowed |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Capability** (`AdvertisedCapabilityV1`) | What the agent CAN DO. The word in the profile, the vault, on chain, in discovery, in every UI. | — |
| **Protocol features** (`ProtocolFeatureSetV1`) | A2A's streaming / push / extensions flags. The wire calls this object `capabilities`, which is the collision. | — |
| **Agent Skill package / playbook** | SKILL.md procedural guidance for a harness. | — |

`skill` without a qualifier means **playbook only**. `skills[]` is A2A's name for capabilities and is
legitimate in exactly two places: `@agenticprimitives/agent-profile/a2a` (the wire types and the projector
that writes them) and a raw-JSON inspector showing a steward the literal document. Anywhere else it is a
defect. Enforced by `pnpm check:capability-vocabulary`.

**The system of record is `profile.capabilities[]`.** The A2A card's `skills[]` and ARD's `capabilities[]`
are projections of it; the A2A projector is their only writer. On chain the record is `atl:capabilities`
(ids only — the chain proves WHICH capabilities are claimed, not their prose). `atl:skills` is that same
rail under its old name: read when the new one is empty, never written. That is a documented migration,
not a fallback (ADR-0013) — same contract, same owner, same value, only the key moved.

What this replaced, and why it mattered: the card editor had a section titled **Capabilities** holding
protocol flags, next to one titled **Skills** holding what the agent can do. Backwards twice over, in the
one screen where a steward decides what the world sees.
